⚡️🇲🇦Moroccan King Mohammed VI appointed Fatima Ezzahra El Mansouri as the country's first female prime minister, after her liberal, monarchy-friendly party (PAM) won the most seats in the September 23 parliamentary elections. 

She is 50 years old and also serves as the mayor of Marrakech.

